+# Incident brief
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September on-call sync.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full database disk
+
+**Impact:** Data intake stopped for about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data was lost.
+
+**Root cause:** A malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the database disk until it refused writes.
+
+**Fix:** A restart that set the bad batch aside, then database cleanup and old-log removal.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done
+- Fix so a bad batch cannot jam ingest (Jonas): open, in review
+- Paging escalation review (no owner named): done 2 September; Elif configured it
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** The public API was unreachable for 47 minutes; nearly all clients failed.
+
+**Root cause:** The API's security certificate expired; its automatic renewal had silently failed since early September, using an outdated credential.
+
+**Fix:** Certificate renewed and API restarted; renewal job repaired and now alerts on failure.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Reminders 14 days before expiry (Priya): done
+- Alert on days left (Priya): open
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open
+- Incident handlers note their steps as they go (Mara): done
